WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
The Fulton County

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.068
Sheriff's Office in Georgia

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.402
says that

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.671
federal investigators are now helping

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.473
track down the origin of threats

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.307
that have been made

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.208
to the grand jury

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.843
that voted to indict former President

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.045
Donald Trump and 18 others this week.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.513
Personal information

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.614
of those members of that

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.383
jury has been posted online.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.451
It has sparked serious safety concerns

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.953
for these everyday Americans.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.321
Who were just simply doing

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.522
their civic duty.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.289
Officials are now

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.291
also tracking threats against officials

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.159
in Fulton County.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.128
They are also increasing security

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.329
for the district attorney there.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.430
Funny Willis.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.165
Joining me now tonight is Robert Pape.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.900
He is a professor of political science

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.568
at the University of Chicago

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.903
who studies and tracks

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.204
these threats to democracy.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:38.972
And that is why, Robert,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.440
you were the perfect person

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.207
to have on this.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.409
I mean, as we know,

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.277
these jurors were just simply

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.345
doing their civic duty.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.913
Anyone could have been called

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.114
to be on this jury.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.016
And now you're seeing anonymous people

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.551
on these mainly far right

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.453
websites calling for violence

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:56.122
against them. I mean, in 20, 23.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.425
Is this just the price you pay

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.326
for playing your part in democracy?

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.062
Well, I'm

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.063
afraid it's the price

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.265
we're going to have to get used to.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.166
This is something

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.601
we must take extremely seriously.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.937
Kate one. For two reasons.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.305
First, our surveys

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.840
at the University of Chicago

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.309
for two years have been tracking

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.011
support for political violence

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.546
in the American public.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.680
And what we're seeing

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.015
is with the indictments,

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.951
what we're seeing is a surge of violence.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:28.388
Support for Donald Trump up 50%

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.724
Today, there are 18 million people

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.827
who agree that the use of force

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.128
is justified

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.629
to restore Donald Trump

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.431
to the presidency.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.967
There is a second reason to be concerned.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.671
There have been multiple attacks

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.407
and multiple armed threats

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.443
against the call them enemies of Trump.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.712
Just over the last year,

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.048
literally a year ago this month,

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.683
there was an assailant

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.853
who attacked the FBI office in Cincinnati

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.122
out of retaliation for the FBI

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.857
raid at Mar a Lago.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:06.092
And just before he died in the shootout,

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.961
he posted on Truth Social

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:08.661
that he wanted

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.829
everybody to know

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.764
that he's doing this for Trump.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.901
The Pelosi attacker last last October,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.803
your audience knows about that.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.471
Just six weeks ago, though,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.606
there was an assailant

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.241
who came to Obama's house

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.676
in Washington, D.C., armed.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.545
And fortunately,

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.080
that threat was diffused.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.515
And of course, last week,

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.583
there was another assailant

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.619
who was making violent threats

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.987
to President Biden.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.955
Threats he had been making in March,

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.891
the police came they talked to him,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:38.825
told him to stop it.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.026
He started again

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.127
the day

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.996
Biden was coming to Utah

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.797
and he brandished a gun.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.766
And rather than stop

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.234
making those threats,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.469
we need to see that

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:53.039
the combination of the rising sentiments,

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.841
violent sentiments for Trump,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.809
that these indictments are triggering

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.444
and the existing pattern

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.946
we already have

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.681
of lethal violence

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.217
against the enemies of Trump.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.218
This really means

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:05.585
we must

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.453
take the threats to the jurors

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.589
very seriously in Georgia

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.192
and be prepared that this won't be over

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.359
for the jurors.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:13.960
I mean,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.595
not even when the trials are over.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.596
And clearly in Georgia,

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.331
I mean, the FBI has been brought in.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:18.865
You referenced

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.399
that there was also

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.767
the woman in Texas

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.468
who was arrested and charged yesterday

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.336
because she had threatened

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.837
to kill a judge

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.506
overseeing one of Trump's cases.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.607
Some people will listen to this

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.042
and say, well, what about the

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.143
the man who showed up?

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.711
Justice Brett Kavanaugh's home.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.013
But I do also you know, you referenced

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:34.981
Trump supporters

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.249
and those who are driven

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.116
and say that, you know,

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.818
the violence justifies the mean.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.587
This is something Trump said today

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.155
about the charges against him.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.892
They want to silence you.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.160
They want to silence you.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.494
And they mean silence.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.331
They are I think they're sick people.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.332
I think they are people

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:55.501
that have no idea how the world works

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.436
and they have no idea

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:59.405
the anger they cause.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.274
What impact do comments like that

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.443
have on his supporters?

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.378
This is inflammatory rhetoric,

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.480
and this is exactly the kind of rhetoric

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.781
that those attackers, the four

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.182
I just

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.216
mentioned,

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.719
were steeped in before their attacks.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.021
But just important to know, one,

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:17.390
that if violent rhetoric can encourage

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.524
political violence

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.026
in calming

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.028
rhetoric can also discourage it.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.731
And we have an important opportunity

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:28.201
next week for political leaders to set

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:31.771
an example on August 23rd next Wednesday.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.873
The Republican primary debate

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.242
is going to be covered nationally.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.544
Every person on that stage

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.312
should be asked

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.747
to stand up

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.248
and stand together

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.951
they're against violent threats,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.752
whether they come

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.787
from the right or the left.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.156
And specifically the threats

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:50.657
we're now

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:51.891
seeing surging

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.394
against the jurors in Georgia.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.462
And if they won't make that pledge

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.631
to stand up to political violence,

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.134
if it really is okay for

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.504
Trump supporters to essentially threaten

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.173
to assassinate those jurors,

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.275
they should be called into account.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:11.944
Why is that? Okay.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.946
We'll see if they are indeed asked that

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.114
or what they have to say about it.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.416
Obviously, it's not an issue

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:17.016
that's going away.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:17.550
Robert Pape,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.484
thank you for joining us

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:21.387
with your expertize tonight. Thank you.

